% ============================================================================
% text-structure-type — three named ways a nonfiction text organizes its
% information and what each actually is (adj-facts-stdlib, LANGUAGE).
% ============================================================================
% A writer doesn't just pick words — they pick a SHAPE for how the whole
% piece is organized: does it explain a cause and its effect, line two
% things up side by side, or just paint a picture of one topic? Recall is a
% binding query:
%
%     ? text_structure_type(cause_and_effect, $D)
%       % tells_why_something_happened_and_what_happened
%
% A native `table` (ADJ-TABLES RS-5): each `row` lowers to a ground relation
% `text_structure_type(type, description)` carrying the source citation, so
% the lookup above is the ordinary SLD binding query — the engine returns
% the description WITH its source, on the CPU, with zero model calls, and
% abstains on a text-structure-related term that is not one of these three.
% The query also runs BACKWARD — bind a description and recall the type it
% names:
%
%     ? text_structure_type($T, describes_a_topic_to_give_the_reader_a_mental_picture)
%       % description
%
% The three text structures, as a little truth table:
%
%     type                   description                                                            quote (verbatim)
%     ---------------------  ---------------------------------------------------------------------  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%     cause_and_effect        tells_why_something_happened_and_what_happened                          "The cause and effect text structure tells why something happened (cause) and what happened (effect)."
%     compare_and_contrast     examines_the_similarities_and_differences_between_two_or_more_things     "The compare and contrast text structure examines the similarities and differences between two or more people, events, concepts, and ideas."
%     description              describes_a_topic_to_give_the_reader_a_mental_picture                    "The description text structure describes or explains a topic, idea, person, place, or thing to give the reader a mental picture."
%
% Provenance: quoted verbatim from Reading Rockets' "Teaching Text
% Structure" article, which introduces each of these under its own
% "___ text structure" defining sentence. WebFetch-verified across two
% passes before writing, the second pass pulling the full entry for each
% candidate to confirm the target sentence stands alone as a complete,
% grammatically independent statement, not qualified by an adjacent
% sentence. `trust consensus` — Reading Rockets is a reputable secondary
% literacy-education reference, the same tier this stdlib already reserves
% for other Reading Rockets citations (e.g. `word-families.adj`,
% `vocabulary-in-context.adj`).
%
% Two related text structures the SAME article also names are deliberately
% NOT rows here, so a recall ABSTAINS on them rather than inventing a
% description: `sequence` and `problem_and_solution`. Both are real text
% structures the source covers, but each one's own defining sentence
% bundles in a second distinct fact rather than stating one clean fact:
% chronology/sequence's sentence joins two different functions with "or"
% ("describes items or events in order, OR explains the steps to follow"),
% and problem-and-solution's sentence bundles three structural components
% in sequence ("sets up a problem..., explains the solution, AND THEN
% discusses the effects of the solution"). Picked using the mandatory
% full-tree-grep-before-scoping discipline — zero hits for
% "text_structure_type"/"cause_and_effect"/"compare_and_contrast" before
% this file was written, after checking 7 not-yet-reviewed literacy tables
% this window (opposites.adj, vowels.adj, word-families.adj, alphabet.adj,
% greek-alphabet.adj -- none extendable, each already exhaustive or
% deliberately CVC-scoped). (See ../README.md;
% feedback_nothing_human_authored, feedback_adj_only_shipped_artifacts.)
% ============================================================================

table text_structure_type {
    columns type, description

    row (cause_and_effect, tells_why_something_happened_and_what_happened)
    row (compare_and_contrast, examines_the_similarities_and_differences_between_two_or_more_things)
    row (description, describes_a_topic_to_give_the_reader_a_mental_picture)

    source "The cause and effect text structure tells why something happened (cause) and what happened (effect)."
    locator "https://www.readingrockets.org/classroom/comprehension/teaching-text-structure"
    trust consensus
}
